/**
 * @mainpage MECHelangelo Code Handover
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section overview What The Code Does
 *
 * MECHelangelo is a ROS 2 Humble workspace for an autonomous gallery robot.
 * The robot uses a differential-drive base to explore a room, detects a person
 * using camera-derived pose tracking, approaches that person to an interaction
 * distance, then mirrors named arm poses for a timed session.
 *
 * The active repository contains the ROS 2 code, Gazebo simulation assets,
 * Raspberry Pi 4 camera/servo reference code, run instructions, generated
 * audio resources, URDFs, meshes, and supporting configuration. Large handover
 * assets such as CAD, videos, datasheets, the bill of materials, and extra
 * reports are no longer in this repository and should be supplied separately.
 *
 * At runtime the system is centred around one behaviour node:
 *
 * - It reads LiDAR, IMU, ultrasonic, and camera-derived human-tracking topics.
 * - It chooses the current high-level state: explore, align, move, approach,
 *   interact, recover, or stop.
 * - It publishes `/cmd_vel` for the base and named arm-pose strings for the
 *   arm controller.
 * - It publishes `/interaction_active` so the Pi 4 or simulation camera knows
 *   when arm mimicry should be enabled.
 *
 * @section student_path Suggested Reading Path
 *
 * New groups should read the project in this order:
 *
 * 1. `README.md` - workspace map and quick commands.
 * 2. This Doxygen main page - architecture and package guide.
 * 3. @ref behaviour_code_guide - detailed guide to the behaviour code,
 *    functions, variables, and state machines.
 * 4. `Run instructions/MECHelangelo_Pi4_Pi5_Setup_Guide.md` - setup notes.
 * 5. `Run instructions/Physical_Robot_Run_Instructions.md` - run procedure.
 * 6. `src/mechelangelo_behaviour/src/behaviour.hpp` - main C++ interface.
 * 7. `src/mechelangelo_behaviour/src/behaviour_physical.cpp` - hardware FSM.
 * 8. `src/mechelangelo_perception/mechelangelo_perception/pi4_bridge.py` -
 *    physical Pi 4 to ROS bridge.
 * 9. The original Pi 4 handover scripts: `pose_debug_v8.py` for the
 *    camera/arm runtime and `servo_test.py` for servo identification and
 *    joint testing.
 *
 * @section layout Repository Layout
 *
 * | Path | Contents |
 * |---|---|
 * | `src/` | Active ROS 2 packages and Pi 4 reference code. |
 * | `Run instructions/` | Setup, physical run, and arm-node handover notes. |
 * | `docs/` | Doxygen config, this main page, and generated Doxygen output. |
 * | `PiBorg_examples/` | ThunderBorg vendor/example scripts for reference. |
 * | `scratch/` | Previous experiments and archived package versions. Not active. |
 * | `README.md` | Short handover entry point. |
 *
 * The active ROS code is under `src/mechelangelo_*`. The `scratch/` folder is
 * intentionally not part of the normal build and should not be treated as the
 * current implementation.
 *
 * @section architecture Overall Architecture
 *
 * @subsection physical_arch Physical Robot
 *
 * The physical robot uses two Raspberry Pis:
 *
 * - Raspberry Pi 5: main ROS 2 computer. Runs the behaviour, base driver,
 *   LiDAR driver, IMU driver, ultrasonic node, and Pi 4 bridge.
 * - Raspberry Pi 4: camera and servo computer. Runs the camera, MediaPipe
 *   pose tracking, KNN arm-pose classifier, and direct LX-16A servo commands.
 *
 * @code
 * Pi 4 camera and servo script
 *   -> HTTP JSON /state
 *   -> pi4_bridge
 *   -> /human_tracking
 *   -> /human_detected
 *   -> /arm/mimicry_right_pose and /arm/mimicry_left_pose
 *   -> mechelangelo_behaviour_physical
 *   -> /cmd_vel
 *   -> mechelangelo_base_driver
 *   -> ThunderBorg motor controller
 *
 * mechelangelo_behaviour_physical
 *   -> /arm/right_pose and /arm/left_pose
 *   -> pi4_bridge/Pi 4 arm logic
 *   -> /interaction_active
 *   -> Pi 4 mimicry gate
 * @endcode
 *
 * The Pi 4 camera does not provide reliable depth. The bridge publishes
 * `distance_m = -1.0`, and the behaviour node uses LiDAR to estimate range to
 * the person.
 *
 * @subsection simulation_arch Simulation
 *
 * The simulation keeps the same high-level topic contract but replaces the
 * physical hardware with Gazebo and laptop camera nodes.
 *
 * @code
 * Gazebo robot camera
 *   -> sim_pi4_state_camera --role tracking
 *   -> /sim_pi4/tracking_state
 *   -> sim_pi4_state_bridge
 *   -> /human_tracking and /human_detected
 *
 * Laptop webcam
 *   -> sim_pi4_state_camera --role mimicry
 *   -> /sim_pi4/mimicry_state
 *   -> sim_pi4_state_bridge
 *   -> /arm/mimicry_right_pose and /arm/mimicry_left_pose
 *
 * mechelangelo_behaviour
 *   -> /cmd_vel
 *   -> Gazebo differential drive plugin
 *   -> /arm/right_pose and /arm/left_pose
 *   -> sim_named_arm_pose_bridge
 *   -> /set_joint_trajectory
 *   -> Gazebo arm controllers
 * @endcode
 *
 * The main simulation launch file is:
 *
 * @code
 * ros2 launch mechelangelo_gazebo mechelangelo_full_mimicry_sim.launch.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section behaviour Behaviour State Machine
 *
 * The `mechelangelo_behaviour` package contains the main robot logic. The node
 * runs a 10 Hz control loop and publishes the final velocity command every
 * cycle.
 *
 * @subsection exploration DVD-Bounce Exploration
 *
 * When no human is detected, the robot explores with a simple wall-bounce
 * strategy:
 *
 * @code
 * SEARCHING -> ALIGNING -> MOVING -> STOPPED -> SEARCHING
 * @endcode
 *
 * - SEARCHING: inspect the filtered LiDAR scan and choose a clear heading.
 * - ALIGNING: rotate until the front arc is clear for the chosen heading.
 * - MOVING: drive forward while checking the front LiDAR cone.
 * - STOPPED: hold briefly after hitting the wall threshold, then choose a new
 *   heading.
 *
 * The physical and simulation behaviours share the same class interface but
 * use separate implementation files:
 *
 * - `behaviour.cpp` - simulation-oriented behaviour.
 * - `behaviour_physical.cpp` - physical robot behaviour with hardware-tuned
 *   approach, voice, and safety logic.
 * - `demo_arm_behaviour.cpp` - stationary demo mode for arm/voice interaction.
 *
 * @subsection human_interaction Human Interaction
 *
 * When `/human_tracking` reports a detected person, the physical behaviour
 * enters its human-interaction logic:
 *
 * 1. Centre the person in the camera image using short turn pulses.
 * 2. Approach slowly while LiDAR confirms the real distance.
 * 3. Settle once the robot is close enough and centred.
 * 4. Publish `/interaction_active = true` for the mimicry session.
 * 5. Forward confirmed arm poses from the mimicry pose topics to
 *    `/arm/right_pose` and `/arm/left_pose`.
 * 6. End the session, reset the arms, and apply a cooldown before detecting
 *    another person.
 *
 * If the camera briefly loses the person, the robot waits for reacquisition.
 * If the target is lost for too long, the node returns to exploration.
 *
 * @section topics Key Topics
 *
 * | Topic | Type | Publisher | Subscriber |
 * |---|---|---|---|
 * | `/scan` | `sensor_msgs/LaserScan` | LiDAR driver or Gazebo | Behaviour |
 * | `/imu` | `sensor_msgs/Imu` | IMU driver or Gazebo | Behaviour |
 * | `/human_detected` | `std_msgs/Bool` | Pi 4 bridge or sim bridge | Behaviour |
 * | `/human_tracking` | `std_msgs/Float32MultiArray` | Pi 4 bridge or sim bridge | Behaviour |
 * | `/arm/mimicry_right_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Pi 4 bridge or sim bridge | Behaviour |
 * | `/arm/mimicry_left_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Pi 4 bridge or sim bridge | Behaviour |
 * | `/cmd_vel` | `geometry_msgs/Twist` | Behaviour or teleop | Base driver or Gazebo |
 * | `/arm/right_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Behaviour | Pi 4 bridge or sim arm bridge |
 * | `/arm/left_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Behaviour | Pi 4 bridge or sim arm bridge |
 * | `/interaction_active` | `std_msgs/Bool` | Behaviour | Pi 4/sim mimicry gate |
 * | `/scan_filtered` | `sensor_msgs/LaserScan` | Behaviour | RViz/debugging |
 * | `/behaviour_obstacle_markers` | `visualization_msgs/MarkerArray` | Behaviour | RViz/debugging |
 * | `/ultrasonic/left`, `/ultrasonic/right` | `sensor_msgs/Range` | Ultrasonic node | Available for behaviour/debugging |
 *
 * `/human_tracking` uses this array layout:
 *
 * | Index | Meaning |
 * |---|---|
 * | `0` | locked/detected, `1.0` or `0.0` |
 * | `1` | centre offset, negative left and positive right by behaviour convention |
 * | `2` | distance in metres, or `-1.0` when camera depth is unavailable |
 * | `3` | tracking valid, `1.0` only when the camera currently sees the person |
 * | `4` | grace active, `1.0` while holding a recently lost target |
 *
 * @section packages Package Guide
 *
 * @subsection pkg_behaviour mechelangelo_behaviour
 *
 * Main C++ state-machine package.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | @ref behaviour_code_guide | Student-friendly explanation of the behaviour package, state machines, functions, and variables. |
 * | `src/behaviour.hpp` | Class interface, state enum, LiDAR segment struct, documented helper methods. |
 * | `src/behaviour.cpp` | Simulation/default autonomous behaviour executable. |
 * | `src/behaviour_physical.cpp` | Physical robot FSM, approach, safety-zone, voice, and arm-session logic. |
 * | `src/demo_arm_behaviour.cpp` | Stationary demo executable for camera-triggered arm and voice interaction. |
 * | `resources/` | MP3 voice lines grouped by event type. |
 *
 * Installed executables:
 *
 * - `mechelangelo_behaviour`
 * - `mechelangelo_behaviour_physical`
 * - `mechelangelo_demo_behaviour`
 *
 * Start with `behaviour.hpp`, then read the `controlLoop()` implementation in
 * the `.cpp` file that matches your target.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_perception mechelangelo_perception
 *
 * Python perception and bridge package.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `pi4_bridge.py` | Polls the Pi 4 HTTP `/state` endpoint and publishes ROS topics. |
 * | `sim_pi4_state_camera.py` | Simulation stand-in for Pi 4 pose tracking and KNN arm classification. |
 * | `sim_pi4_state_bridge.py` | Combines simulated tracking and mimicry states into behaviour topics. |
 * | `sim_named_arm_pose_bridge.py` | Converts named poses to Gazebo `JointTrajectory` messages. |
 * | `sim_interaction_gate.py` | Optional simulation gate node for older pipelines. |
 * | `dual_ultrasonic.py` | GPIO driver for two HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensors. |
 * | `config/pose_knn_right.json` | Right-arm KNN training data. |
 * | `config/pose_knn_left.json` | Left-arm KNN training data. |
 *
 * The physical Pi 4 logic is not a ROS node in the current workspace. Follow
 * `Run instructions/Physical_Robot_Run_Instructions.md` for the original Pi 4
 * runtime flow: `pose_debug_v8.py` runs the camera/arm state server, and
 * `servo_test.py` is used separately for identifying servos and testing joint
 * angles. `pi4_bridge.py` converts the Pi 4 HTTP state into the ROS topic
 * contract used by behaviour.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_base mechelangelo_base_driver
 *
 * Python driver for the PiBorg ThunderBorg motor controller.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `base_driver.py` | Subscribes to `/cmd_vel`, applies limits/deadband, and sends motor power commands. |
 * | `ThunderBorg.py` | ThunderBorg hardware API used by the driver. |
 * | `config/base_driver.yaml` | Wheel separation, speed limits, motor inversion, watchdog, and LED settings. |
 *
 * The driver includes a command watchdog. If `/cmd_vel` stops arriving, motor
 * power is set to zero.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_lidar mechelangelo_lidar_driver
 *
 * Python YDLIDAR X4 serial driver.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `lidar_driver.py` | Opens the serial LiDAR connection and publishes `/scan`. |
 * | `config/lidar_driver.yaml` | Serial port, frame ID, scan settings, and mounting offset. |
 *
 * Behaviour applies its own filtering and segmentation after receiving
 * `/scan`.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_imu mechelangelo_imu_driver
 *
 * Python Sense HAT driver.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `imu_driver.py` | Publishes IMU and environmental sensor topics. |
 * | `config/imu_driver.yaml` | Frame ID and driver parameters. |
 * | `config/RTIMULib.ini` | RTIMULib sensor-fusion configuration. |
 * | `sense_hat/` | Bundled Sense HAT Python support code. |
 *
 * @subsection pkg_teleop mechelangelo_teleop
 *
 * Keyboard control utilities.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `teleop_keyboard.py` | Generic keyboard `/cmd_vel` publisher. |
 * | `teleop_keyboard_real.py` | Physical-robot keyboard teleop variant. |
 * | `teleop_keyboard_thunderborg.py` | ThunderBorg-oriented keyboard control helper. |
 *
 * Use teleop only after confirming the emergency stop and motor direction.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_description mechelangelo_description
 *
 * URDF and mesh package.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `urdf/mechelangelo_final.urdf` | Full robot description. |
 * | `urdf/mechelangelo_base.urdf` | Base-only description. |
 * | `urdf/mechelangelo_arm.urdf` | Single-arm test description. |
 * | `urdf/mechelangelo_dual_arms.urdf` | Dual-arm test description. |
 * | `meshes/` | Base, wheel, arm, and sensor meshes. |
 *
 * @subsection pkg_gazebo mechelangelo_gazebo
 *
 * Gazebo Classic simulation package.
 *
 * | File or folder | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `launch/mechelangelo_full_mimicry_sim.launch.py` | Main full simulation pipeline. |
 * | `launch/empty_gallery.launch.py` | Empty gallery world with robot. |
 * | `launch/mechelangelo.launch.py` | Gallery world with robot and props. |
 * | `launch/environment.launch.py` | Gallery world without the full robot pipeline. |
 * | `launch/environment_arm.launch.py` | Arm-focused simulation environment. |
 * | `worlds/` | Gazebo world files. |
 * | `models/` | Gallery props, humans, floors/walls, and robot models. |
 * | `config/arm_controllers.yaml` | Gazebo arm controller configuration. |
 *
 * @subsection pkg_bringup mechelangelo_bringup
 *
 * Physical robot launch package.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `launch/physical_autonomous.launch.py` | Current physical bringup: LiDAR, IMU, base driver, ultrasonic, Pi 4 bridge, and physical behaviour. |
 * | `launch/demo_launch.py` | Stationary demo launch. |
 * | `launch/robot.launch.py` | Older generic bringup. It currently references `mechelangelo.urdf.xacro`, which is not present in this workspace. |
 *
 * Use `physical_autonomous.launch.py` as the hardware entry point unless you
 * deliberately update the older `robot.launch.py` file.
 *
 * @subsection pi4_code Pi4_code
 *
 * Reference code for the Raspberry Pi 4 camera and servo side.
 *
 * | File | Role |
 * |---|---|
 * | `pose_debug_corrected.py` | Workspace reference script for camera, MediaPipe pose extraction, KNN arm classification, HTTP state serving, and LX-16A servo commands. |
 * | `arm_pose_test.py` | Servo/pose testing helper. |
 *
 * This folder is not installed as a ROS package by `colcon`. For physical
 * robot operation, keep using the original Pi 4 instructions:
 *
 * @code
 * python3 pose_debug_v8.py
 * python3 servo_test.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * Do not run `servo_test.py` at the same time as `pose_debug_v8.py`, because
 * both can try to access the same servo serial connection.
 *
 * @section launch_files Main Launch Files
 *
 * Simulation:
 *
 * @code
 * ros2 launch mechelangelo_gazebo mechelangelo_full_mimicry_sim.launch.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * Physical robot:
 *
 * @code
 * ros2 launch mechelangelo_bringup physical_autonomous.launch.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * Stationary demo:
 *
 * @code
 * ros2 launch mechelangelo_bringup demo_launch.py
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section maintenance_notes Handover Notes
 *
 * - Keep `README.md` and this page limited to files that are actually present
 *   in the repository.
 * - Keep large non-code handover assets outside the repository or provide
 *   them through a separate storage link.
 * - Treat `scratch/` as historical context, not production code.
 * - If package entry points are added or removed, update this page and the
 *   relevant `setup.py` or `CMakeLists.txt` in the same change.
 * - Regenerate Doxygen before handover with `doxygen docs/Doxyfile`.
 */
